   "source": [
    "# Comparative Sequence and Structural Analysis of Clinical HBB Variants\n",
    "**Focus:** Wild-Type (HbA), Sickle Cell (HbS), and Hemoglobin C (HbC)  \n",
    "**Author:** Muhammad Junaid  \n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Project Overview & Clinical Scope\n",
    "Point mutations at the identical codon in the human beta-globin (*HBB*) gene produce distinctly different clinical hemoglobinopathies:\n",
    "* **Sickle Cell Disease (HbS, `rs334`):** Codon 6 missense mutation ($Glu6Val$) driving deoxy-state polymerization, red cell sickling, and vaso-occlusion.\n",
    "* **Hemoglobin C Disease (HbC, `rs33930363`):** Codon 6 missense mutation ($Glu6Lys$) causing intraerythrocytic crystal formation and cellular dehydration without sickle polymers."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ed4688e4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Biological Question & Working Hypotheses\n",
    "\n",
    "### Biological Question\n",
    "> **How do single-nucleotide missense substitutions at the identical codon (mature residue 6) of human beta-globin (*HBB*) induce distinct physicochemical perturbations (hydropathy vs. charge), and how does the native 3D spatial microenvironment in deoxyhemoglobin (PDB: `1A3N`) explain their divergent pathological mechanisms (polymerization vs. crystallization)?**\n",
    "\n",
    "### Working Hypotheses\n",
    "1. **Sickle Cell (HbS — Glu6Val):** Replacing negatively charged Glutamate with non-polar Valine creates an abnormal hydrophobic protrusion on the solvent-accessible surface of the $\\beta$-chain without disrupting tertiary folding, enabling non-covalent docking into adjacent deoxy-tetramers ($Phe85/Leu88$ pocket).\n",
    "2. **Hemoglobin C (HbC — Glu6Lys):** Replacing Glutamate with basic Lysine introduces a positive charge inversion ($\\Delta Q = +2$) without substantial hydropathy gain, precluding sickle polymer docking while promoting electrostatic crystal nucleation and solute loss.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Methodological Boundary:** PDB `1A3N` represents the wild-type crystallographic ground state. Structural coordinates describe the native microenvironment of Glu6 and do not represent computationally simulated mutant tertiary folds."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "98a523de",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Dataset Ingestion & Quality Control\n",
    "We ingest the wild-type human *HBB* mature coding sequence (cDNA clone `CR536530.1`) and verify the local PDB structure (`1A3N.pdb`)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "0c326a46",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "✓ Sequence QC Passed | Accession: CR536530.1 | Length: 444 nt | Codon 7: GAG\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from Bio import SeqIO\n",
    "\n",
    "# Multi-path resolver\n",
    "candidates = [Path.cwd(), Path.cwd() / \"data\", Path.cwd().parent / \"data\"]\n",
    "data_dir = next((p for p in candidates if (p / \"human_hbb_cds.fasta\").exists() and (p / \"1A3N.pdb\").exists()), None)\n",
    "\n",
    "if data_dir is None:\n",
    "    raise FileNotFoundError(\"Required files 'human_hbb_cds.fasta' and '1A3N.pdb' not found in workspace.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "fasta_path = data_dir / \"human_hbb_cds.fasta\"\n",
    "pdb_path = data_dir / \"1A3N.pdb\"\n",
    "\n",
    "record = SeqIO.read(fasta_path, \"fasta\")\n",
    "wt_cds = str(record.seq).upper()\n",
    "\n",
    "# QC validation checks\n",
    "assert record.id == \"CR536530.1\", f\"Unexpected accession: {record.id}\"\n",
    "assert set(wt_cds) <= set(\"ACGT\"), \"Non-canonical nucleotide bases detected.\"\n",
    "assert len(wt_cds) % 3 == 0, \"CDS length is not a multiple of 3.\"\n",
    "assert wt_cds.startswith(\"ATG\"), \"Missing standard ATG start codon.\"\n",
    "assert wt_cds[-3:] in {\"TAA\", \"TAG\", \"TGA\"}, \"Missing canonical stop codon.\"\n",
    "assert wt_cds[18:21] == \"GAG\", f\"Expected GAG at codon 7, found {wt_cds[18:21]}\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"✓ Sequence QC Passed | Accession: {record.id} | Length: {len(wt_cds)} nt | Codon 7: {wt_cds[18:21]}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f32c5e98",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Controlled In-Silico Mutagenesis & Translation\n",
    "Post-translational processing in human erythrocytes removes the initiator Methionine (Met1). Therefore:\n",
    "- **cDNA Coordinates:** Codon 7 (nucleotides 19–21: `GAG`)\n",
    "- **Mature Protein & PDB (`1A3N`):** Residue Position 6"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "8faf8feb",
